 CheckRequestTarget←{
     ⍝ ⍵ ←→ Request(s)
     ⍝ ← ←→ 0; signals a DOMAIN ERROR when a "RequestTarget" is not simple character data
     ⍝ Composing the request line from such a target would produce a nested or numeric one,
     ⍝ which no server can parse, and the client would then sit waiting for a reply that is
     ⍝ never coming - which looks like a hang and says nothing about what went wrong.
     ⍝ Called before a connection is opened, so that a refused request leaves nothing behind.
     ∧/{(0=10|⎕DR ⍵)∧1≥≢⍴⍵}¨(,⍵).RequestTarget:0
     '"RequestTarget" must be a simple character vector'⎕SIGNAL 11
 }
